      "title": "Rust method-vs-module-level: pub use re-export of inherent methods fails with E0432",
      "severity": "info",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": [
        "Initial attempt used `pub use ce_write::{save_counterexample_bundle, ...}` in parent module \u2014 failed with E0432 \"no save_counterexample_bundle in counterexample_storage::ce_write\" because methods inside `impl SessionStore` blocks are not module-level items.",
        "Fix: drop the `pub use` lines. Methods are still callable via `<SessionStore>::method_name` or `instance.method_name()` regardless of which file the impl block lives in.",
        "Verified all real callers use `.method_name(...)` form via grep across crates/ \u2014 zero path-qualified `counterexample_storage::method_name(...)` call sites exist in the workspace."
      ]
    }
